Hermes Agent attribution for agent_files/{disk,selection,scan}.rs, tools/memory.rs,
tools.rs memory descriptions and components/providers.rs memory curation guidance
Source: https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent
Revision: f3ef9db68332063a3625661f3a9b259f60abdb4e

Adapted agent/prompt_builder.py source selection (_agents_md_directory_chain,
_agents_md_candidates, _hermes_md_candidates, _claude_md_candidates,
_cursorrules_candidates, discover_context_files, load_soul_md) and
 tools/threat_patterns.py::_PATTERNS / scan_for_threats, focused all-scope patterns.
Selected threat IDs: prompt_injection, sys_prompt_override, disregard_rules,
bypass_restrictions, html_comment_injection, hidden_div, translate_execute,
deception_hide, exfil_curl, exfil_wget, read_secrets. Context/strict-scope
patterns are intentionally omitted. Fixtures are invented local strings,
including short representative attack/identity strings; no private files.

Intentional differences: Anima-branded ANIMA.md/.anima.md project sources and
anima manifest kinds; configured-root capabilities only, no ambient home/cwd;
derived profile namespace; all files including SOUL screened; blocked candidates
fall through; whole sources above 65,536 Unicode scalars excluded instead of
scanning a prefix; full-width ASCII fold only rather than Python NFKC; no trust
exceptions; SHA-256 content-free manifest. Fixed bounded Rust regex matching is
advisory and can miss threats or reject legitimate discussion. Ordinary identity
prose remains accepted. Immutable snapshots do not freeze the filesystem.

An OS-stuck blocking read cannot be killed. The five-second caller deadline
includes admission; two process-wide permits remain held until actual worker
completion. Later loads fall back if both workers are stuck. Cancellation never
publishes a late result. No claim of physical thread termination is made.

M17 memory correction adaptation (revision 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899):
tools/memory_tool.py::_pin_matched_entries and tools/memory_tool_store.py::_find_unique_match,
_locate pin replacement to the full reviewed entry and refuse stale or ambiguous
targets. Anima ports that replacement boundary into native Rust: exact record ID
plus exact expected content, checked under a same-agent memory write lock through
durable save with MemoryMutation rollback. It preserves unrelated record fields
and evidence links. No fuzzy matching, profile-file imports, Python execution,
global memory authority, removal, batch edits, or upstream fail-open gate behavior
are imported. Existing Anima tool grants and write approvals still apply.

M18 memory curation adaptation (revision 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899):
tools/memory_tool.py and agent/prompt_builder.py inform the concise static habit
of keeping compact declarative durable facts, preferences and standing context,
skipping temporary progress/logs, avoiding duplicate facts and keeping procedures
in existing skill workflows. Native Rust owner-scoped lexical context selection
and bounded quoted excerpts are Anima implementations, not Hermes storage or
snapshot semantics. Stored facts are evidence; current requests and tool approval
policy remain authoritative. Excerpts require memory_search for exact correction
input. No extra model/embedding call, automatic skill write, upstream Python
execution, private profile/config/environment/keyring/token read, or broad memory
lifecycle behavior is imported. Lexical selection does not claim semantic recall
quality or Hermes parity.

M21 native action-witness adaptation (revision 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899):

hermes_state_messages.py::append_message (lines389-423) informs preparation outside
the critical writer transaction, guarded stable tool-call correlation, awaited
write acknowledgement and aborting the turn on critical write failure. Native
Rust bounded run action receipts use Anima's control-plane persistence and owner
authority; they are separate from the final committed chat transcript. No Python,
upstream SQLite schema, compression/turn leases, private profile/config/keyring or
token bridge is imported. Anima adds fail-closed parallel admission and conservative
started/unknown-effect recovery; receipts do not establish exactly-once effects.

M30 memory removal adaptation (revision 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899):
tools/memory_tool.py remove dispatch and tools/memory_tool_store.py::remove/_locate
support removing a selected entry while pinned full reviewed text rejects stale
writes. Anima applies that intent to one explicitly granted own visible Fact:
exact ID and complete expected content under the existing native write lock,
MemoryMutation persistence and established delete_memory citation cleanup. This
is hard removal from active legacy memory, not revisioned tombstones, complete
erasure or automatic consolidation. No fuzzy substring/batch matching, Python
runtime, upstream profiles or credentials are copied. Existing Write policy
and per-agent grants remain authoritative; no automatic grant is added.
M31 owner reviewed-delete adaptation (revision 1fd18277267152893a8a24792b79213e7ca3f899):
The same public pinned-entry remove intent used in M30 now applies to owner
memory-record DELETE when complete expectedContent is supplied. Compare the
exact reviewed text under the native memory write lock before mutation/save;
stale text returns a content-free conflict. Empty-body legacy owner deletion
remains. No fuzzy matching, revision/ABA guarantee, complete erasure, upstream
Python runtime or private profiles are imported.

